\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab Saviour , when in dust to Thee
\par \pard\li360       Low we bow the adoring knee;
\par \pard            When, repentant, to the skies
\par            Scarce we lift our weeping eyes;
\par             O by all Thy pains and woe
\par            Suffered once for man below,
\par              Bending from Thy throne on high,
\par            Hear our solemn litany.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab By Thy helpless  infant years,
\par \pard\li720 By Thy life of want and tears 
\par By Thy days of sore distress \tab\tab 
\par \pard\fi360\li360 In the savage wilderness
\par By the dread , mysterious hour
\par Of the insulting tempter's power
\par Turn O turn a favouring eye
\par Hear our solemn litany
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab By the sacred grief that wept
\par \pard\li720 O'er the grave where lazarus slept,
\par By the boding tears that flowed
\par Over Salem's loved abode,
\par By the anguished sigh that told
\par Treachery lurked within Thy fold :
\par From Thy seat above the sky,
\par Hear our solemn litany.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\tab By Thine hour of dire despair,
\par \pard\li720 By Thine agony of prayer,
\par By the Cross, the nail, the thorn,
\par Piercing spear and torturing scorn ;
\par By the gollm that veiled the skies
\par O'er the dreadful sacrifice :
\par Listen to our humble cry,
\par Hear our solemn litany.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.\tab By Thy deep expiring groan,
\par \pard\li720 By the sad sepulchral stone,
\par By the vault whose dark abode
\par Held in vain the rising God :
\par O from earth to heaven restored,
\par Mighty re-ascended Lord,
\par Listen, listen to the cry
\par Of our solemn litany.
\par Amen. 
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

